              "file_path": "/home/jovyan/adi_wdir/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/sf_triggers/models/simple_baseline.py"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "f407e746-5b8e-415e-aca4-1f51f703e84d",
      "raw_time": false,
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "",
      "mentions": [],
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "time": 1789584474.4175723
    },
    {
      "body": "Two separate bugs in `forward()`, from your edit:\n\n**1. The `rearrange` pattern drops the linear layer's output channel dim.** `self.linear(x)` on shape `(B*H*W, 13)` produces `(B*H*W, 1)` \u2014 that trailing `1` is the linear layer's output feature, not a dim you can drop. Your pattern `\"(b h w) -> b h w\"` declares only 1 input dim, but the tensor has 2, hence `EinopsError: expected 1 dims. Received 2-dim tensor`.\n\n**2. There's a leftover duplicate `self.linear(x)` in the final `return`.** After the (fixed) rearrange, `x` is already the per-pixel prediction \u2014 but the function then feeds it through `self.linear` *again*. That's a second bug that would surface right after fixing #1: `self.linear` expects a `(..., 13)`-shaped input, not the `(B, H, W)` you'd have by then.\n\nFix: keep the channel dim through the rearrange, and return `x` directly instead of re-applying the linear layer.",
      "type": "msg",
      "time": 1789584530.7596931,
      "raw_time": false,
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "mentions": [],
      "id": "c9c2bdb5-00fd-4013-b324-9170a4d2671a"
    },
    {
      "metadata": {
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "title": "Edit models/simple_baseline.py",
            "raw_input": {
              "old_string": "        x = x[\"ts\"]\n        B,C,T,H,W = x.shape\n\n        # Collapse input stack spatially and take absolute value for strictly positive flare fluxes\n        x = x.abs()#.mean(dim=[3, 4])\n        print('====================')\n        # Rearrange in preparation for linear layer\n        print(x.shape)\n        x = rearrange(x, \"b c t h w -> (b h w) (c t)\")\n        print(x.shape)\n        x = self.linear(x)\n        print(x.shape)\n        x = rearrange(x,\"(b h w) ->  b h w \",b=B,h=H, w=W)\n        print(x.shape)\n        \n        \n\n        return self.linear(x)",
              "replace_all": false,
              "new_string": "        x = x[\"ts\"]\n        B, C, T, H, W = x.shape\n\n        # Take absolute value for strictly positive flare fluxes; predict per-pixel\n        # instead of spatially pooling, so the output matches the (B, 1, H, W) mask target.\n        x = x.abs()\n\n        # Rearrange in preparation for linear layer\n        x = rearrange(x, \"b c t h w -> (b h w) (c t)\")\n        x = self.linear(x)\n        x = rearrange(x, \"(b h w) c -> b c h w\", b=B, h=H, w=W)\n\n        return x",
              "file_path": "/home/jovyan/adi_wdir/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/sf_triggers/models/simple_baseline.py"
            },
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01RrB2svMtE54fHobs4sTLB8",
            "raw_output": "The file /home/jovyan/adi_wdir/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/sf_triggers/models/simple_baseline.py has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context \u2014 no need to Read it back)",
            "kind": "edit",
            "locations": [
