    },
    {
      "body": "That command needs interactive stdin to paste your key, which doesn't work through this tool. Run it yourself in a real terminal instead \u2014 pick whichever you prefer:\n\n**Option A \u2014 interactive (recommended, key stays only in your terminal history):**\n```bash\nconda activate surya_ws\nwandb login\n```\nIt'll prompt you to paste the key from https://wandb.ai/authorize.\n\n**Option B \u2014 non-interactive, one line:**\n```bash\nwandb login <YOUR_API_KEY>\n```\n\nEither way it writes the key to `~/.netrc`, and every `WandbLogger` call in this repo (the notebooks, `3_finetune_template_1D.py`) will pick it up automatically \u2014 no code changes needed.\n\nA couple of things specific to this repo worth checking once you're logged in:\n\n- `configs/config_script.yaml` for `sf_triggers` has `wandb_project: sf_triggers` and `wandb_entity: null` (line 223-224) \u2014 `null` means runs log to your personal account. If you want them under a team/org instead, set `wandb_entity` to that team name.\n- The notebook's WandB markdown cell mentions being invited to a project \u2014 if you're meant to log to a shared team account rather than personal, let me know the entity/org name and I can set `wandb_entity` in the config for you.\n\nLet me know once you've run `wandb login` and I can verify it worked (e.g. by checking `wandb status` or doing a quick test run).",
